# Frontend (Vite, React 18, TypeScript, Tailwind v4, shadcn/ui)

## Structure (`ARCHITECTURE.md` §11)
- `pages/` thin route components; logic in `features/<feature>/`; shared UI in `components/`.
- Routes are registered in `app/router.tsx` (integrator-owned); replace your page file only.

## Data and state (`ER-18`)
- API types only from `lib/api/schema.d.ts` (generated from `openapi.yaml`). No hand-written API types.
- All requests through `lib/api/client.ts` (adds auth, `Accept-Language`, `X-Booking-Token`, `X-Client-Id`).
- Server data: TanStack Query. Booking flow: Zustand store (sessionStorage). Access token in memory only.
- Mocks: your feature's MSW file `mocks/handlers/<feature>.ts`, shaped exactly like the contract.

## UI
- Text only via i18n keys in your namespace, in **both** `vi` and `en` (`ER-16`). Errors: map `code` → `errors:<CODE>`.
- Tokens and type classes from `DESIGN.md` §3–4; no hex colours, no inline `style={{ fontFamily }}` (`ER-19`).
- `SeatMap`, `TicketCounter`, `SnackPicker`, `ShowtimeList`, `MovieCard`, `HoldCountdown` are presentational: props in, callbacks out, no fetching or routing inside (`ER-17`).
- Every screen handles loading, empty and error states; interactive elements are keyboard reachable and labelled.

```tsx
// ❌ <p style={{ color: '#d4a843' }}>Còn 5 ghế</p>
// ✅
<p className="text-primary">{t('booking:seatsLeft', { count: 5 })}</p>
```

- Money/dates via `lib/money.ts` and `lib/dates.ts`; never `toLocaleString` ad hoc.
